Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:37:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] process completion custody: an explicit kill settles
 the owed notice; review follow-ups

Review 5880232292 on PR #1675 (request changes):
- Blocker: a kill with consume_output=True that loses the finish race to the reader
  rewrote the receipt keeping the delivery obligation, so the next gateway start
  re-armed a notice the caller already had. The kill-path rewrite now settles it for an
  explicit kill and keeps (never re-creates) it for a bulk cleanup kill.
- The kill-path read+write and the watcher's acknowledgement both run under the
  registry lock (settle_completion), so a rewrite cannot resurrect a settled obligation.
- One malformed owed receipt no longer aborts recovery of the owed receipts after it.
- Count pruning (MAX_RETAINED_RESULTS) keeps owed receipts; age pruning (7 d) is past
  the 48 h obligation cap.
- The subagent handoff note is redacted before it reaches the receipt; the watcher
  route fields are the checkpoint's own (persisted there verbatim already).

